      "writtenOn": "2019-08-14T21:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I *think* strlen() on a constant string will be optimized as a constant, so you could use strlen() here and still wouldn\u0027t have a variable-length array. This BUILD_CHECK_INLINE seems to show that is what is happening:\n\n  \tuint8_t info[strlen(info_prefix) + sizeof(user_id)];\n\n\tBUILD_CHECK_INLINE(sizeof(info), sizeof(info_prefix) - 1 + sizeof(user_id));\n\nUsing strlen() just makes it consistent with strlen(info_prefix) that is used later in the function.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "28a3fb70473b30bdf4273b67973dbbe4b5e0af9b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cf2d5f4_c5a7464c",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor_crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-14T23:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for this! I think using strlen here would make the code look like variable-length array to people (including norvez@). Maybe let\u0027s still use sizeof to make it clear that it\u0027s not VLA at the first glance?",
      "parentUuid": "0a06d394_11fb6194",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "28a3fb70473b30bdf4273b67973dbbe4b5e0af9b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a11cd0e_37bcf6c7",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor_crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1158184
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-15T00:13:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t mind either way, as long as we make it clear that it\u0027s not a VLA. I *think* the fact that strlen() knows the value at compile time for constant strings is a result of GCC using a builtin (and I think clang has a similar one) but I didn\u0027t see it officially documented in https://www.gnu.org/software/libc/manual/html_node/String-Length.html\n\nI don\u0027t mind using strlen() -it does help readability!- if:\n- we comment that this is done on purpose with the compile-time optimisation in mind and is not a VLA\n- we add some compile-time assertion, something like Tom\u0027s BUILD_CHECK_INLINE, to ensure that it won\u0027t break if we ever change the compiler options (or the compiler itself...)\n\nDoes that make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "1cf2d5f4_c5a7464c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "28a3fb70473b30bdf4273b67973dbbe4b5e0af9b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a7d6e445_710be345",
        "filename": "common/fpsensor/fpsensor_crypto.c",
